  "claim_boundary": "This is a hardware-local certificate for four registered, direction-sensitive two-workload GPU co-location trajectories. Target completion includes initialization, the canonical outer-loop work, checkpoints/final save, and natural exit. Resident service is the counter increment strictly inside the target start/end markers divided by the full overlap duration. One wave-maximum split-conformal margin jointly covers both functionals for all four actions. Every row also hash-verifies the pre-launch nvidia-smi snapshot and rejects undeclared load on any registered GPU, so a hash-bound one-second sidecar covers the complete target interval, records aggregate host load as an endogenous action diagnostic, bounds available memory, and rejects high-CPU same-user processes outside the two controlled process groups. Thus same-GPU co-location rows do not silently absorb undeclared host/PCIe contention. It neither populates the legacy workload/profile index nor extrapolates to unmeasured mixtures, hardware, or future workloads.",
